# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# w0m — the ESTATE WORKSPACE repo (T294).
#
# This repo holds what sits BESIDE the seven repos and belonged to none of them:
# estate-root agent config, editor workspaces, and cross-repo reports. It is
# emphatically NOT a monorepo — every repo below stays its own repo, and this
# file is the guarantee. Sweeping seven repos into an eighth is the failure AC2
# exists to prevent, so the exclusions come first and are proven by
# `git add -A && git status --porcelain` staging none of them.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── the seven repos are excluded via .git/info/exclude, NOT here ─────────────
# 🔴 A directory pattern here is read by tools BELOW this repo. Git stops applying .gitignore at a
# repo root, but osv-scanner does not: with `/wom7web/` in this file it walked up from inside
# wom7web, applied the pattern, concluded the whole repo was ignored, and reported "No package
# sources found" — exit 128 in ALL SEVEN repos at once. A security gate, silently disabled estate-wide
# by one line in a parent .gitignore.
#
# So the nested-repo exclusions live in `.git/info/exclude`, which is inside .git/ and therefore
# invisible to anything walking the worktree. That file is not versioned, so `scripts/install_excludes.py`
# is the versioned surface and re-running it is what makes this reproducible — the same reasoning
# install_hooks.py already records for `.git/hooks/`.

# ── archives and scratch (~1.4 GB), and client material ──────────────────────
# _in carries prospect/client documents. The KB content policy keeps client work
# out of shared tiers, so it is excluded regardless of this repo's visibility.
/_ds_arc/
/_ds_arc_pack/
/_ext/
/_in/
/_t99_arc/

# ── generated ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/graphify-out/
/supabase/.temp/

# ── large or machine-local state inside otherwise-tracked config ─────────────
.serena/cache/
.headroom/memory.db

# ── a bug artefact, not a directory anyone meant to create ───────────────────
# A tool wrote an unexpanded VS Code variable as a literal path.
${input:db_path}

.DS_Store
*.log
